    {
        "id": "9f1aacee0d2ed0fe",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "0977fce194365578",
        "name": "Init order",
        "info": "Startup\n\n1. CONSTANTS\n2. CONFIG\n3. PREFS\n4. HOST\n5. UTILS\n6. DEVICES\n7. STATE\n8. Validate Startup\n9. Startup Complete\n\nCONSTANTS has no dependencies.\nCONFIG may use constants.\nPREFS may depend on configuration (default values, storage location, etc.).\nHOST is independent and can be collected early.\nUTILS may use constants/config.\nDEVICES will almost certainly use CONSTANTS, CONFIG, and possibly PREFS.\nSTATE is last because it represents the initial runtime state after everything else exists.",
        "x": 260,
        "y": 760,
        "wires": []
    },
    {
        "id": "3b8cb6717d2bc39d",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "0977fce194365578",
        "name": "HOST",
        "info": "HOST\n├── hostname\n├── os\n│   ├── name\n│   ├── version\n│   └── kernel\n├── nodeRed\n│   ├── version\n│   └── uptime\n├── nodejs\n│   └── version\n├── hardware\n│   ├── model\n│   ├── architecture\n│   └── serialNumber\n├── network\n│   ├── hostname\n│   ├── ipAddress\n│   └── macAddress\n└── startupTime\n",
        "x": 990,
        "y": 680,
        "wires": []
    },
    {
        "id": "a09aac1ae2293994",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "0977fce194365578",
        "name": "CONSTANTS",
        "info": "RULES:\nCONSTANTS are values that may be changed by the developer or administrator, \nbut only intentionally as part of the system's design. They are not runtime preferences.\n\nLWT_DOWN; 0\nLWT_UP; 1\nDEV_DWN_2_MINS: 2\nHEARTBEAT: 3?",
